# A second `print` of a new expression at the same stop answers in under
# 100 ms on a program of 20,000 functions, the size of a large compiler
# package's image. The bound is the recv's: it starts when the expression
# is sent and fails with the time it took ("recv deadline exceeded after
# N ms") when the answer is later. Before, each new expression compiled
# the program again: this session's second print took 2,701 ms at 20,000
# functions and 2,200 ms at 2,000 (the dev jet of a3fa36e63f).
# Each print compiles the package's sources cut to the functions it
# reaches (DebugCompile.jet jet_cli_debug_eval_sliced), with no compile of
# the program. The first print reads the package's items and decides the
# session's Core binding, which the second takes without reading a named
# toolchain tree's Core again (jet_cli_debug_eval_core). Both read
# `total`, 0 at the stop, and call the program's own functions: f_k(x) is
# (x + k) % 1000.
# gen/gen.jet writes prog.jet: run's first call, the stop, is line 100003.
fixture: SecondPrintAnswersUnder100ms.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run gen/gen.jet -- 20000
exit: 0
stdout: = ""
session debug line: jet debug prog.jet
env: PATH={work}/no-tools
send debug: "break prog.jet:100003"
send debug: "c"
recv debug line until ~ "Breakpoint hit  prog.jet:100003  in run()" timeout 600s # the image builds and the program runs to the stop
send debug: "print f_1(total)"
recv debug line until ~ "f_1(total) = 1" timeout 600s # the first print reads the package's items and decides the Core binding
send debug: "print f_2(total) + f_3(total)"
recv debug line until ~ "f_2(total) + f_3(total) = 5" within 100ms # a second, new expression answers in under 100 ms
send debug: "c"
recv debug line until ~ "Program finished" timeout 600s # the evaluations left the program's run unchanged
close debug
exit: 0
